Root cause of the error: oShape.VisProperties does not exist on an AnyObject reference. In CATIA's API, visual properties (colour, transparency, etc.) must be set through Selection.VisProperties — you first add the feature to the Selection, then call VisProperties on the Selection object.

What changed in v4:

The colouring block went from this (wrong):

vb
Dim oVisProp As VisPropertySet
Set oVisProp = oShape.VisProperties   ' ERROR - AnyObject has no VisProperties
oVisProp.SetRealColor 255, 255, 0, 1
To this (correct):

vb
oSel.Add oShape                        ' add to selection first
Dim oVP As VisPropertySet
Set oVP = oSel.VisProperties           ' VisProperties on the Selection object
oVP.SetRealColor 255, 255, 0, 1        ' apply yellow
oSel.Clear                             ' clear, colour is now permanent
oSel.Add oShape                        ' re-add so it stays selected at the end

