Claude responded: The error is on oBox.
The error is on oBox.SetFocus — a hidden TextBox cannot receive focus. The fix is to use the DataObject clipboard approach instead, which is the correct way to copy text to clipboard in CATIA VBA without needing a visible control.

Replace the entire btnCopy_Click with this:

vb
Private Sub btnCopy_Click()
    Dim sReport As String
    Dim oData   As DataObject
    sReport = BuildReport()
    Set oData = New DataObject
    oData.SetText sReport
    oData.PutInClipboard
    MsgBox "Report copied to clipboard!", vbInformation, "Copied"
End Sub
Why this works: DataObject is part of the MSForms library which is already loaded when you have a UserForm — no extra references needed. It copies text directly to the Windows clipboard without needing any visible control or focus trick.

